3
00:00:11,168 --> 00:00:14,548
(Sheldon:)Now, remember, Newton realized
that Aristotle was wrong...

4
00:00:14,714 --> 00:00:17,304
(Sheldon:)...and force was not necessary
to maintain motion.

5
00:00:17,466 --> 00:00:20,756
(Sheldon:)So let's plug in our 9.8 meters
per second squared...

6
00:00:20,928 --> 00:00:24,218
(Sheldon:)...as A and we get force--
Earth gravity.

7
00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:27,730
(Sheldon:)--equals mass times
9.8 meters per second per second.

8
00:00:27,894 --> 00:00:32,274
(Sheldon:)So we can see that MA equals MG
and what do we know from this?

9
00:00:36,444 --> 00:00:41,494
Uh.... We know that Newton
was a really smart cookie.

10
00:00:43,159 --> 00:00:46,039
Oh, is that where Fig Newtons
come from?

11
00:00:46,746 --> 00:00:50,086
(Sheldon:)No, Fig Newtons are named
after a small town in Massachusetts.

12
00:00:50,791 --> 00:00:53,501
-No, don't write that down.
-Sorry.

13
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:56,210
(Sheldon:)Now, if MA equals MG...

14
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:58,470
(Sheldon:)-...what does that imply?
-I don't know.

15
00:00:58,633 --> 00:01:01,213
What--? But--?
How can you not know? I just told you.

